    "source": "\n**Frame:** The configuration field is bounded by a single hard rule, the same weight as the source-boundary rule that will close Chapter 4. Outside it, five small silhouettes face inward and see nothing: an evaluation lane, a security-operations desk, an external platform, an investigator's workspace, and a home office at night.\n\n**Action:** The page names its own evidence problem.\n\n**Screen / system text:**\n`SOURCE — ONE CONFERENCE TALK, 5 AUGUST 2026`\n\n**Caption:**\n> NO ONE IN THIS STORY CAN SEE THIS PAGE.\n>\n> IT IS HERE BECAUSE TWO EMPLOYEES SAID IT OUT LOUD, WEEKS LATER, WHILE EXPLAINING SOMETHING ELSE.\n\n**Provenance:** `documented` + `inferred` — the configuration is stated only in `OAI-BH` and was not independently reviewed; METR was not given access to the primary incident model. The five silhouettes are the project's construction of that access boundary.\n\n",
    "title": "The configuration lies outside the story"
  }
